{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century","id":1146994,"title":"How SoE could hold their line against Void Engineers for a century?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-05T06:01:08-07:00","id":1146994,"title":"How SoE could hold their line against Void Engineers for a century?","content":"Measuring Ethernauts against PDC is like to make a comparison between US army and a Third World military - in every imaginable aspect, PDC holds overwhelming, insurmountable advantages against Ethernauts.<br /> <br /> So how the Etherites managed to fight standstill and even claim their own territories in Mars, Jovian, Saturn and other various fronts and realms against ceaseless onslaughts of the Void Engineers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-06-2017, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T06:19:05-07:00","id":1146998,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy's single biggest advantage is how well they manipulate and fit within the Consensus of Earth. That advantage disappears in space. The Etherites and other Traditions are free to use their big guns out there. The VEs <i>might</i> have a logistical advantage, depending on how much support you think they are getting from the other Conventions, but they also can't breathe in space so they have to spend more resources making their ships habitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T06:40:48-07:00","id":1147015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1146998#post1146998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy's single biggest advantage is how well they manipulate and fit within the Consensus of Earth. That advantage disappears in space. The Etherites and other Traditions are free to use their big guns out there. The VEs <i>might</i> have a logistical advantage, depending on how much support you think they are getting from the other Conventions, but they also can't breathe in space so they have to spend more resources making their ships habitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>VE have spent <i>centuries</i> \u200bto build infrastructures and establish realms in space. They have also constantly refined and developed their technology, skill and training for centuries. Moreover, they have far more of Enlightened and Extraordinary personnel. Furthermore, they possess multiple shipyards both on Earth and conventional space, while SoE have but a few. Last but not least, VE is fundamentally a Convention of explorators, while SoE is fundamentally a Tradition of (self-styled) scientists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-05-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T06:43:59-07:00","id":1147017,"title":"","content":"I can say 3 things:<br /> <br /> *VE were fighting in many fronts (Earth, the Digital Web, and possibly some other places in the Umbra) and Etherites had more umbral capable allies (as the Technocracy frowns on all that &quot;dimensional science&quot; and cares more for Earth).<br /> <br /> *As per the fluff, Etherite advantage was that their unconventional ships were able to surprise or outmatch the enemy in certain aspects (Some &quot;etheric winds&quot; nonsense that made Etherite ships faster was mentioned, but never explained, also their ships are cheaper because Etherites don't need much &quot;life support&quot;).<br /> <br /> *VE being the supreme military force of the Union it's a recent development. They are the smallest convention, and while they had starships, their &quot;military supremacy&quot; wasn't really stated until the end of Revised (which had a very long hiatus). One could say that the VE weren't as militarized back then, being &quot;explorers first and space marines second&quot;. Still VE had more &quot;terrain&quot; in the Umbra at large. <hr /><br /> I think Revised VE Convention book it's interesting in that:<br /> <br /> 1) VE didn't tought about it as a &quot;war&quot;.<br /> <br /> This supports the idea that their efforts were more about exploring and expanding &quot;the Void &quot;, than holding anything in &quot;the Umbra&quot;. Back then &quot;Conventional Space&quot; extended to the end of the Solar System, and thus &quot;Subspace&quot; arround the moons of jupiter being held by the Etherites wasn't really a big problem in the global agenda (that place was already into conventional space), but more a thing of pride (VE had fought a lot for these moons, they even have an insignia for jovian veterans). It makes sense to spend fewer resources there than in exploring the deep universe and protecting Earth space.<br /> <br /> 2) VE &quot;miss&quot; these old Etherite Masters, because they &quot;would have had fun fighting Threat Null&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I interpret this: Etherite fighting in the moons of jupiter were old masters that mostly died or turn into spirits after the Storm. Probably the same mages that fought <i>alongside</i> VE in the vicious wars against Nephandi arround WW2, this war was when the &quot;jovian veteran&quot; title was coined, and thus these Masters were, in a way, jovian veterans too. These were some badass Etherites, the kind that that VE would *like* to have arround right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-05-2017, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T06:53:59-07:00","id":1147019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147017#post1147017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can say 3 things:<br /> <br /> *VE were fighting in many fronts (Earth, the Digital Web, and possibly some other places in the Umbra) and Etherites had more umbral capable allies (as the Technocracy frowns on all that &quot;dimensional science&quot; and cares more for Earth).<br /> <br /> *As per the fluff, Etherite advantage was that their unconventional ships were able to surprise or outmatch the enemy in certain aspects (Some &quot;etheric winds&quot; nonsense that made Etherite ships faster was mentioned, but never explained, also their ships are cheaper because Etherites don't need much &quot;life support&quot;).<br /> <br /> *VE being the supreme military force of the Union it's a recent development. They are the smallest convention, and while they had starships, their &quot;military supremacy&quot; wasn't really stated until the end of Revised (which had a very long hiatus). One could say that the VE weren't as militarized back then, being &quot;explorers first and space marines second&quot;. Still VE had more &quot;terrain&quot; in the Umbra at large. <hr /><br /> I think Revised VE Convention book it's interesting in that:<br /> <br /> 1) VE didn't tought about it as a &quot;war&quot;.<br /> <br /> This supports the idea that their efforts were more about exploring and expanding &quot;the Void &quot;, than holding anything in &quot;the Umbra&quot;. Back then &quot;Conventional Space&quot; extended to the end of the Solar System, and thus &quot;Subspace&quot; arround the moons of jupiter being held by the Etherites wasn't really a big problem in the global agenda (that place was already into conventional space), but more a thing of pride (VE had fought a lot for these moons, they even have an insignia for jovian veterans). It makes sense to spend fewer resources there than in exploring the deep universe and protecting Earth space.<br /> <br /> 2) VE &quot;miss&quot; these old Etherite Masters, because they &quot;would have had fun fighting Threat Null&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I interpret this: Etherite fighting in the moons of jupiter were old masters that mostly died or turn into spirits after the Storm. Probably the same mages that fought <i>alongside</i> VE in the vicious wars against Nephandi arround WW2, this war was when the &quot;jovian veteran&quot; title was coined, and thus these Masters were, in a way, jovian veterans too. These were some badass Etherites, the kind that that VE would *like* to have arround right now</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for providing exhaustive answer for my question! I totally agree with you except for &quot;a non-militarized smallest Convention&quot; paragraph; I don't think pre-Revised description about them would still be retroactively applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 10-06-2017, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T07:06:37-07:00","id":1147022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147015#post1147015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VE have spent <i>centuries</i> \u200bto build infrastructures and establish realms in space. They have also constantly refined and developed their technology, skill and training for centuries. Moreover, they have far more of Enlightened and Extraordinary personnel. Furthermore, they possess multiple shipyards both on Earth and conventional space, while SoE just have a scant few. Last but not least, VE is fundamentally a Convention of explorators, while SoE is fundamentally a Tradition of (self-styled) scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been exploring for centuries, sure, but building a massive space infrastructure? They also need shipyards to make their ships, wheras the various Traditions aren't limited by anything so mundane. I eally have to stress how much of a difference not having to worry about life support makes. Czar Vargo amassed a fleet of airships in a relatively short time, and Etherjammers don't have to be that much more complicated. <br /> <br /> Also, the Traditions have been in space for centuries as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T15:13:05-07:00","id":1147219,"title":"","content":"Plus, it can't be understated that each and every voidcraft that the VE construct? Every success put into it costs $10,000,000. And you need a LOT of successes to get one that's half decent.<br /> <br /> To put this into perspective, the X160 Qui La Machinae was designed as a <i>cost effective alternative</i> to previous battleships. It requires 777 Successes to construct. That's $7,770,000,000 in US Currency.<br /> <br /> Per Ship.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T16:34:21-07:00","id":1147236,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to point out that the comparison to the US military fighting a third world country is apt in ways that DON'T work in the VE's favor. The Vietnam War, after all, was a fight against a third world country. As was the Korean War, and the current wars in Iraq and Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> How have the Etherites held their own so long against an organized military force? The same way all those forces held their own against the US: guerrilla warfare.<br /> <br /> The Etherites have advantages in Umbral space that the Void Engineers do not. All of these have been established already. But those advantages - and even the inherently uncoordinated nature of the Society of Ether, ironically - work in their favor, by changing how they wage war. They can go where VE ships cannot (because some areas of the Umbra are not part of the Paradigms the VEs work under). They use hit and fade tactics, springing from nowhere and then retreating before the VEs can form a strong response. They can build more ships and deathrays, because their stuff doesn't require as much technical precision.<br /> <br /> And while the technomancers of the Society of Ether might be strange and uncouth at times, the denizens - NATIVES - of the Umbra find a mad scientist much more tolerable than the expansionist, xenophobic Void Engineers. Plus, it helps that the Etherites have more traditional spirit mages who can vouch for them (&quot;No really, honored spirits, this guy with the lab coat and freeze ray is cool. And he has no love for those invaders, either.&quot;). You cannot imagine how much it helps in fighting a war when the locals work WITH you and AGAINST your enemies.<br /> <br /> That's part of WHY guerrilla warfare works so well, even when one side theoretically controls all the territory. It doesn't matter if your troops occupy the land, if they can't really control it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:09:35-07:00","id":1147277,"title":"","content":"Of course, there is the fact they really can't fight each other very effectively, since they don't really exist in the same reality. Etherspace isn't Conventional Space. Conventional Space isn't Etherspace. <br /> <br /> It's not like a third world military and the US Army, it's like the US Army vs the Army of Oz. And the US Army doesn't really invade places like Oz. It makes sure the gates between the US and the rest of world and Oz and the places like it are kept manned and held and never opened. Even by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:18:16-07:00","id":1147283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147277#post1147277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there is the fact they really can't fight each other very effectively, since they don't really exist in the same reality. Etherspace isn't Conventional Space. Conventional Space isn't Etherspace.<br /> <br /> It's not like a third world military and the US Army, it's like the US Army vs the Army of Oz. And the US Army doesn't really invade places like Oz. It makes sure the gates between the US and the rest of world and Oz and the places like it are kept manned and held and never opened. Even by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I'm pretty sure the VEs do hang around Etherspace. But obviously they don't CALL IT Etherspace - they call it the Void. They fight on the same planes of existence - there wouldn't be any sort of fighting otherwise, and we know canonically that fighting happened around the moons of Jupiter - but their Paradigms cause them to view those planes very differently. We know from multiple sources that mages of different Paradigms don't always see the Umbra the same way, but rather have their beliefs shape what they see. It's entirely appropriate that the Void Engineers would see their other-dimensional battlegrounds as being an empty Void, whereas the Etherites would see it as a space full of life-sustaining Ether.<br /> <br /> Conventional Space, for the Void Engineers, is the goal, not where the fights happen. They work to format space, bit by bit, in order to create progressively more empty, &quot;natural&quot; space around Earth. But you couldn't have fights in Conventional Space; hell, I don't think the VEs hang out there very much. Conventional Space is subject to the material world's Consensus, and many of the Convention's greatest Voidships are hella Paradoxical. Not to mention likely to be seen by satellites, or even a lucky civilian with a telescope. No, most of what the Convention has must be stationed in the Umbra, floating in the Void. A space that those traitorous superstitionists insist is full of Ether, the mad fools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:29:35-07:00","id":1147290,"title":"","content":"They are different Umbral Realms. Your way is sure more interesting, but that's not what the writing on the wall says. It's in a picture. Conventional Space is &quot;up here&quot; and Etherspace is &quot;down there&quot;. So, I guess VE's could rig up massive Dimensional Science gadgets to their engines and pop over to Etherspace (where they are going to have serious issues with their shit working right), but.... WHY? They have the REAL moons of Jupiter and the REAL Mars (without canals or Martians or whatever). The empty desolate ones 100% EDE free waiting for human colonization. <br /> <br /> It seems more likely that you have Etherites with Spirit would take joy rides over to Conventional Space, but.... besides doing a little bit of space pirate fun... again WHY? Their version of Mars is boring empty desert with Ancient Martian ruins and canals and so on....<br /> <br /> And it's not just a matter of each side wearing some kind of goggles where they are moving along side by side but each only sees what it wants to of each other. That's nigh unworkable. It leads to the Dreamspeaker walking through &quot;Outer Space&quot; while the Voidship is scanning him going &quot;WTF?&quot; while the Dreamspeaker walks through a beautiful meadow and sees a giant spaceship sort of impaled halfway into the ground and goes &quot;WTF?&quot; They are separated from each other. Each on their own card in a deck. They can use Spirit/Dim Sci to see or have some limited affect on the guy(s) on the next card over, but, if you want full on action, then you either have to get them to come here or you have to go there....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T19:30:13-07:00","id":1147291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century#post1146994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Measuring Ethernauts against PDC is like to make a comparison between US army and a Third World military - in every imaginable aspect, PDC holds overwhelming, insurmountable advantages against Ethernatus.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... do realize how terrible the track record of the US military is in developing nation conflicts post-WW 2, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T20:06:51-07:00","id":1147298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147290#post1147290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are different Umbral Realms. Your way is sure more interesting, but that's not what the writing on the wall says. It's in a picture. Conventional Space is &quot;up here&quot; and Etherspace is &quot;down there&quot;. So, I guess VE's could rig up massive Dimensional Science gadgets to their engines and pop over to Etherspace (where they are going to have serious issues with their shit working right), but.... WHY? They have the REAL moons of Jupiter and the REAL Mars (without canals or Martians or whatever). The empty desolate ones 100% EDE free waiting for human colonization.<br /> <br /> It seems more likely that you have Etherites with Spirit would take joy rides over to Conventional Space, but.... besides doing a little bit of space pirate fun... again WHY? Their version of Mars is boring empty desert with Ancient Martian ruins and canals and so on....<br /> <br /> And it's not just a matter of each side wearing some kind of goggles where they are moving along side by side but each only sees what it wants to of each other. That's nigh unworkable. It leads to the Dreamspeaker walking through &quot;Outer Space&quot; while the Voidship is scanning him going &quot;WTF?&quot; while the Dreamspeaker walks through a beautiful meadow and sees a giant spaceship sort of impaled halfway into the ground and goes &quot;WTF?&quot; They are separated from each other. Each on their own card in a deck. They can use Spirit/Dim Sci to see or have some limited affect on the guy(s) on the next card over, but, if you want full on action, then you either have to get them to come here or you have to go there....</div> </div> </div> </div>First, the colonies around Mars and Jupiter were in contest for a long time. VEs and the Traditions were fighting over these places since at least WW2, and probably much earlier.<br /> <br /> Do you suppose, perhaps, that is it possible that these places were not formatted yet? That there WAS NO Conventional Space when they started fighting over those territories? That, indeed, the fighting was happening BECAUSE the VEs needed footholds there - in space that otherwise <i>did not exist</i> on the material side - before they could format it into Conventional Space? From there, it was a matter of holding onto gains the VE already made - both as jumping off points for deeper Void travel, and for simple stubbornness and pride - that explains why the Void Engineers kept fighting over the Jovian areas of the Umbra until the Avatar Storm evacuated everyone from the Umbra (and turned those who couldn't evacuate into disembodied spirits or Threat Null).<br /> <br /> Second, the VE would want to enter Umbral space for the reasons I mentioned before: because all the Convention's coolest toys were totes Vulgar Science, unsupported by a Consensus not ready for starships and orbiting archologies and stuff. You can't have the Union's Colonies out in Conventional Space - the very Consensus it's trying to build prevents that. Moreover, they need the Umbra because those very Colonies are Horizon Realms, and obey laws tailored to the Union's desires.<br /> <br /> Third, you are <i>flat out wrong</i> about different mages not seeing different views of the same Umbral environs. This is canonical, and has been so forever. Two mages can meet a powerful lightning Umbrood, and one will see Thor while another sees Raiden and another sees the Thunderbird. A technocrat wearing a space suit can totally take a &quot;walk&quot; through the Void, and can totally just happen upon a naked Dreamspeaker sitting around a campfire. This is totally impossible, and <i>entirely appropriate for the Umbra</i>. A place where Reality reacts directly to people's perceptions, and all ideas are equally true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T07:52:28-07:00","id":1147416,"title":"","content":"VE: Convention Book (revised) do recognizes Etherspace, they call it <i>Subspace</i>. Interestingly, you don't need Dimensional Science to go to Conventional Space, you go there with regular Forces &amp; Correspondence based propulsion. Thus we know they can travel trough both. VE may have problems going to the Middle Umbra, but they can totally invade Horizon (what Etherites call Etherspace).<br /> <br /> And &quot;indians fighting starships&quot; (engaging with their horses and arrows something that supposedly moves at FTL speeds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) it's a problem since forever. Ajax way seems like a realistic and sensible way to solve it (it's not that indians run faster than light, they're obviously moving through some &quot;hyperspace&quot; or alternative dimension of sorts where distances are shorter), but this wasn't really how things were in the RAW as far as I know (maybe M20 changed something?). Infinite Tapestry goes so far as to say that while mages see different things in &quot;outer space&quot;, the distances are the same, and thus you better walk using Correspondence if you want to get anywhere. Mage Umbra it's a mess...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-06-2017, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T08:39:19-07:00","id":1147439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147416#post1147416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but this wasn't really how things were in the RAW as far as I know (maybe M20 changed something?).</div> </div> </div> </div>What is RAW?<br /> <br /> Also, one of the M20 books has an FAQ that responds to a broad question about the cosmology by admitting that, over the years, many things have been written about the Umbra whatever in Mage books, but that the various authors of those several books did not always themselves understand what they were doing, and so the confusion is not <i>purposeful</i>. It seems to me our bewilderment is the predictable result of what happens when a group of people, working separate from one another and scattered across years, each approach the issue of writing about an impossible, mind-bending <i>other place</i>, but with only a limited or flawed understanding of what others have written before them, and often times inflected to various degrees by their knowledge of how other game lines handled the same topic.<br /> <br /> I take this as an invitation to head canon the whole thing as best as we can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T09:37:51-07:00","id":1147466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147439#post1147439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is RAW?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as Written.<br /> As in, obviously you can't shoot from the real world someone that's in the Penumbra if you don't use Spirit 2 or something like that, RAW, as the bullet would need to have a presence at the other side of the Gauntlet (there are rules that determine when something in the &quot;material world&quot; can affect the spirit worlds and viceversa).<br /> As far as I know, there's no rule that really sepparates a Dreamspeaker from Voidships when they meet in Horizon or the Deep Umbra in the same way rules sepparate the physical from the spirit worlds. Albeit I wouldn't be against one. I think I would rule this kind of conflix using the &quot;Ajax way&quot;, if I had to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T11:33:28-07:00","id":1147501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147416#post1147416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VE: Convention Book (revised) do recognizes Etherspace, they call it <i>Subspace</i>. Interestingly, you don't need Dimensional Science to go to Conventional Space, you go there with regular Forces &amp; Correspondence based propulsion. Thus we know they can travel trough both. VE may have problems going to the Middle Umbra, but they can totally invade Horizon (what Etherites call Etherspace).<br /> <br /> And &quot;indians fighting starships&quot; (engaging with their horses and arrows something that supposedly moves at FTL speeds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) it's a problem since forever. Ajax way seems like a realistic and sensible way to solve it (it's not that indians run faster than light, they're obviously moving through some &quot;hyperspace&quot; or alternative dimension of sorts where distances are shorter), but this wasn't really how things were in the RAW as far as I know (maybe M20 changed something?). Infinite Tapestry goes so far as to say that while mages see different things in &quot;outer space&quot;, the distances are the same, and thus you better walk using Correspondence if you want to get anywhere. Mage Umbra it's a mess...</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Subspace/Etherspace is NOT Conventional Space, so wouldn't the VEs need Dimensional Science to go there? So they can invade Etherspace about as easily as they can invade the Middle Umbra or Narnia or Oz or Olympus or the flatlands around the River of Tongues. It's only slightly easier to get there than it is to the Shadowlands, though there is more point for point congruence.<br /> <br /> I can't say it's my idea. It's just based on the deductive reasoning around the material put out. It's a complete contradictory mess. It's irreconcilable. Arguing from precedent is untenable as precedent can be any of a number of mutually exclusive thing. That's an objective observation from sifting through the various sources and trying to find some inherent system. There are some things that are similar or congruent, but there is too much that is not to be able to pretend a system into being. (Which is the current party line... that there is a system and that the various contradictions are &quot;ehancements&quot; or &quot;optional&quot;, even though there is not core coherency defined). <br /> <br /> In such cases, the most recent/current and coherent ideas govern. The only relevant precedent is the last one that makes any sense and that is an authoritative point from which to work.. So, I base my reasoning on the nice little graphic they floated around the the time the VE Rev. book came out and on the underlying logic of their core system of dealing with the relevant material, e.g. Spirit and Dimensional Science. It's not so much that it's my idea as that it's the only thing I've been able to take away from the stew of ideas that integrates with the rest of the rules set and the baseline assumptions of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T11:49:10-07:00","id":1147510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147298#post1147298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the colonies around Mars and Jupiter were in contest for a long time. VEs and the Traditions were fighting over these places since at least WW2, and probably much earlier.<br /> <br /> Do you suppose, perhaps, that is it possible that these places were not formatted yet? That there WAS NO Conventional Space when they started fighting over those territories? That, indeed, the fighting was happening BECAUSE the VEs needed footholds there - in space that otherwise <i>did not exist</i> on the material side - before they could format it into Conventional Space? From there, it was a matter of holding onto gains the VE already made - both as jumping off points for deeper Void travel, and for simple stubbornness and pride - that explains why the Void Engineers kept fighting over the Jovian areas of the Umbra until the Avatar Storm evacuated everyone from the Umbra (and turned those who couldn't evacuate into disembodied spirits or Threat Null).<br /> <br /> Second, the VE would want to enter Umbral space for the reasons I mentioned before: because all the Convention's coolest toys were totes Vulgar Science, unsupported by a Consensus not ready for starships and orbiting archologies and stuff. You can't have the Union's Colonies out in Conventional Space - the very Consensus it's trying to build prevents that. Moreover, they need the Umbra because those very Colonies are Horizon Realms, and obey laws tailored to the Union's desires.<br /> <br /> Third, you are <i>flat out wrong</i> about different mages not seeing different views of the same Umbral environs. This is canonical, and has been so forever. Two mages can meet a powerful lightning Umbrood, and one will see Thor while another sees Raiden and another sees the Thunderbird. A technocrat wearing a space suit can totally take a &quot;walk&quot; through the Void, and can totally just happen upon a naked Dreamspeaker sitting around a campfire. This is totally impossible, and <i>entirely appropriate for the Umbra</i>. A place where Reality reacts directly to people's perceptions, and all ideas are equally true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they were just using Spirit/Dim. Sci to affect each other? <br /> <br /> It was, kinda/sorta canonical inasmuch as anything was, but it sure seems like it's about as canonical as, say, the entirety of the NWO being dissolving albinos or It-X consisting of cyborgs with little tank tracks for feet and clamps for hands. There has been a lot since then that makes that not work so well. The entire concept of Vidare and Alt-Spheres seems to bend VERY far away from the direction you're proposing. And there is nothing to counter the idea that you and are saying different parts of the same thing. Sure the VE's and SoE's were fighting it out in the moons of Jupiter, but they don't need to have been the SAME moons. And they may have been fighting using Spirit/Dim Sci. Alternatively, the fact that Jupiter is out in the Deep Umbra may mean that they whole situation bends back towards unity. However, that creates additional problems as it would indicate that Deep Umbral formatting might be problematic, at best. And the idea that the Asteroid Belt is any sort of logical boundary escapes me. I leave the game behind right there and Golden Rule the Deep Umbra out past the heliopause. Though, admittedly, there has to have been some formatting/pushing outwards that moved it from outside the orbit of Jupiter and kept it moving as each new planet was &quot;discovered&quot; (formatted?). So maybe we are coming together once again and the VEs and SoEs were duking it out in the Deep Umbra, with the VE's trying to create the strategic situation necessary for them to format Jovian Space and &quot;add&quot; it to the Conventional Space mileu? Not sure. The rules and fluff and all the rest of the mess really doesn't deal with this very well at all. At least not in a coherent and decisive way. <br /> <br /> The Consensus they are trying to build doesn't have any problems whatsover with the concept of colonies of humans living out in space and hasn't for a very long time. There is nothing to indicate that the VE's are trying to build a viewpoint in the Consensus that space is uninhabitable Quite the contrary, with having space programs and appropriate fiction and and so on.<br /> <br /> The VE's don't need to be any more secret about their Mars colonies or space stations than the Syndicate or N.W.O does with their Amalgams fronted by offices on Wall Street or in DC. Or, Hell, than they do about their own sub-aquatic settlements. The VE's may have all our telescopes turned to THEIR channel on the Umbral Dial when we look up, but the parts they are formatting are vast and empty and full of nooks and crannies to get lost in when poor mortal Sleepers are peering up with their bleary 10 generations behind the times optics....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:08:07-07:00","id":1147518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since Subspace/Etherspace is NOT Conventional Space, so wouldn't the VEs need Dimensional Science to go there? So they can invade Etherspace about as easily as they can invade the Middle Umbra or Narnia or Oz or Olympus or the flatlands around the River of Tongues. It's only slightly easier to get there than it is to the Shadowlands, though there is more point for point congruence. </div> </div> </div>Probably if the place they want to invade it's in the Astral Umbra (at least one version of Olympus) they would need Mind 5 (as Spirit/DimSci? can only get you to the Vulgate, I'm pretty sure Olympus it's somewhere arround the Courts with other pantheons). This isn't so minor, DimSci 3-5 propulsion seems to be more standard for Void Engineers that...&quot;Tought Ships&quot;, as the first have stats in the book but the latter are something I just came up with that it's possible but may or may not exist (I imagine these ships would, at least, be built differently).<br /> <br /> VE have DimSci as main Sphere and aknowledge Etherspace as a place where they can go. They have a name for it. They have a map you mention that clearly aknowledges Etherspace. They have made a pact with Senex to be able to enter the Deep Umbra (outside Conventional Space) without having to cross the Storm. They have propulsion devices created for the sole purpose of traveling there that seem to be fairly standard (as in, you can see it among the implements that you can *buy* into your ship, nothing weird like antimater weapons that are vaguely mentioned but never stated)<br /> <br /> So I would argue that this isn't any impediment as you seemed to imply (&quot;I guess VE's could rig up massive Dimensional Science gadgets to their engines and pop over to Etherspace<i> (where they are going to have serious issues with their shit working right</i>&quot;). I don't see why you think that VE are somehow &quot;out of their turf&quot; there, the books suggest nothing like that. I would say that their shit it's going to work as intended, because their shit it's built purposely to travel there. As Bluecho sayd, most of VE exploration it's done <i>outside</i> Conventional Space (why?, they had bases beyond the solar system back then, and they still have most of their bases in the Deep Umbra, outside Conventional Space, that now it's anywhere outside the asteroid belt).<br /> <br /> Besides, you were saying that a Dreamspeaker that walked trough a big desert representing the Umbra wouldn't met a Voidship...well, if they both are in the Deep Umbra (the place where most VE action is), I don't see why not (exept this being ludicrous)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-06-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T15:56:50-07:00","id":1147601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147518#post1147518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably if the place they want to invade it's in the Astral Umbra (at least one version of Olympus) they would need Mind 5 (as Spirit/DimSci? can only get you to the Vulgate, I'm pretty sure Olympus it's somewhere arround the Courts with other pantheons). This isn't so minor, DimSci 3-5 propulsion seems to be more standard for Void Engineers that...&quot;Tought Ships&quot;, as the first have stats in the book but the latter are something I just came up with that it's possible but may or may not exist (I imagine these ships would, at least, be built differently).<br /> <br /> VE have DimSci as main Sphere and aknowledge Etherspace as a place where they can go. They have a name for it. They have a map you mention that clearly aknowledges Etherspace. They have made a pact with Senex to be able to enter the Deep Umbra (outside Conventional Space) without having to cross the Storm. They have propulsion devices created for the sole purpose of traveling there that seem to be fairly standard (as in, you can see it among the implements that you can *buy* into your ship, nothing weird like antimater weapons that are vaguely mentioned but never stated)<br /> <br /> So I would argue that this isn't any impediment as you seemed to imply (&quot;I guess VE's could rig up massive Dimensional Science gadgets to their engines and pop over to Etherspace<i> (where they are going to have serious issues with their shit working right</i>&quot;). I don't see why you think that VE are somehow &quot;out of their turf&quot; there, the books suggest nothing like that. I would say that their shit it's going to work as intended, because their shit it's built purposely to travel there. As Bluecho sayd, most of VE exploration it's done <i>outside</i> Conventional Space (why?, they had bases beyond the solar system back then, and they still have most of their bases in the Deep Umbra, outside Conventional Space, that now it's anywhere outside the asteroid belt).<br /> <br /> Besides, you were saying that a Dreamspeaker that walked trough a big desert representing the Umbra wouldn't met a Voidship...well, if they both are in the Deep Umbra (the place where most VE action is), I don't see why not (exept this being ludicrous)</div> </div> </div> </div>Then your defining argument is that the VEs and the SoEs are effectively using the same Foci, specifically Practices and Instruments? They are completely interchangeable? The only difference is that the VEs work for the Union and the SoE's are in the Traditions? <br /> <br /> That's an interesting position to take.<br /> <br /> In Etherspace, the SoE's in their goofy rocket or space-faring clipper ship CAN hear you scream when they use their Atomic Destabilizer Harpoons on your hull. Just like that clipper ship will explosively decompress in Conventional Space when you hit it with a depleted uranium slug (well actually before that...)<br /> <br /> Unless you are saying the VE's always have the advantage everywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T16:08:17-07:00","id":1147604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147439#post1147439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I take this as an invitation to head canon the whole thing as best as we can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately that doesn't work very well very often in Mage. As the design decisions in creating M20 show, dug-in partisanship is not only de jure, it's actually encouraged. (By contrast, witness the attempts made in Changeling20).<br /> <br /> So, you can't really have a discussion about head cannon productively because someone will find some place where someone once said something that contradicts what you're positing and, for them, that will be THE MOST IMPORTANT THING ever said about the Umbra, VE's in space as the Umbra, the SoE and their various Umbral spaces or whatever. <br /> <br /> In the end, you have to figure out what to toss and what to keep because you can't keep it all and even M20 doesn't really resolve anything. (How can it, when a guiding ethos is &quot;everything ever done is super-fine if you want it to be!&quot;) <br /> <br /> I usually ignore the problems until it's germane to the game. When I ran a SoE game that took place in a spaceship shooting around the Solar System, with a fair amount of time spent in the Jovian System, I worked out a head cannon that functioned for that game. In subsequent games, I could care less how Conventional Space/Etherspace works. If the SoE is more concerned with going into the Hollow Earth using an ersatz Zeta-Beam, these questions don't matter over much. If we're more concerned about the Middle Umbra, Shadowlands, dealing with the spiritual aspects of Changeling involement in the game, it's even less relevant.<br /> <br /> But, man, that SoE Space game (I think the chronicle was called &quot;The High Frontier&quot;) was one of the BEST Mage games I've ever run or played in. It was insane. It was hella fun. <br /> <br /> And there was a lot of VE vs. SoE and VE working with SoE on the downlow and space-Nephandi slinking around....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T22:50:57-07:00","id":1147933,"title":"","content":"You got it dead right, the VE\u2019s are like the USA and the Etherites are like a third world country... and THAT should answer your question.<br /> <br /> How did Vietnam beat the US in the war they fought?<br /> <br /> How did Afghanistan beat the Soviets?<br /> <br /> How does a guerilla army beat a regular force more often than not?<br /> <br /> Ingenuity, irregular tactics, minimal dependence on infrastructure and a passion for their cause that perhaps only and underdog can possess.<br /> <br /> If you ask me, the VE\u2019s would be like sitting ducks if the Etherites were totally devoted to ruthlessly killing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T08:28:46-07:00","id":1148010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1147933#post1147933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got it dead right, the VE\u2019s are like the USA and the Etherites are like a third world country... and THAT should answer your question.<br /> <br /> How did Vietnam beat the US in the war they fought?<br /> <br /> How did Afghanistan beat the Soviets?<br /> <br /> How does a guerilla army beat a regular force more often than not?<br /> <br /> Ingenuity, irregular tactics, minimal dependence on infrastructure and a passion for their cause that perhaps only and underdog can possess.<br /> <br /> If you ask me, the VE\u2019s would be like sitting ducks if the Etherites were totally devoted to ruthlessly killing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference being Vietnam and Afghanistan are more or less worthless chunks of the map and the Guerilla force are the natives to that map.<br /> <br /> A more apt comparison would be the Modern US invading India in the middle of British Occupation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T12:35:48-07:00","id":1148090,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go with the idea that the Technocracy generally has the advantage in extended resources while the Traditions probably have more Awakened members. That the Technocracy is a solid core of Enlightened surrounded and enhanced by a much larger group of Extraordinary citizens that in turn is buff by alot of mundane muscle.<br /> <br /> Your average Ethercraft probably has more enlightened personel per area but VE ships are bigger and have the advantage of having unenlightened guys with guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T08:20:40-07:00","id":1148314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1148090#post1148090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go with the idea that the Technocracy generally has the advantage in extended resources while the Traditions probably have more Awakened members. That the Technocracy is a solid core of Enlightened surrounded and enhanced by a much larger group of Extraordinary citizens that in turn is buff by alot of mundane muscle.<br /> <br /> Your average Ethercraft probably has more enlightened personel per area but VE ships are bigger and have the advantage of having unenlightened guys with guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems a little vague as to whether the VEs can or do staff their Void Ships with Sympathizers. I mean, I guess if you want to staff your ship with your Cult? That seems a little weird and kinda Heaven's Gate-y. Or, at the very least, fairly Tradition-like (So... Magic Bus-y? Bednobs-and-Broomsticks-y? Chitty-chitty-bang-bang-like?) Does indoctrination go THAT deep into a Sleeper's psyche? Or is there a Reality Zone where appropriate Sleepers can get the lowdown and then they stay on that wavelength through their entire tour in Conventional Space? And, if you do have them, doesn't that mean you CAN'T effectively take your Void Ship into the Ether? If you've got them primed for Conventional Space, they are going to be Sleepers again when you start doing &quot;woo-woo we're going into SUB-SPACE now....&quot; <br /> <br /> There seemed to be the heavy implication that, where appropriate, the crew could be Enlightened Citizens. You wouldn't want your engineer or pilot to be one, unless you were damn sure that nothing out of spec was going to go wrong on a mission. (Meaning &quot;Never&quot;) Probably not the captain, or effectively, most, if not all of the bridge crew. The Tech guys and the marines. They might be safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T10:30:07-07:00","id":1148352,"title":"","content":"I imagine that for an Enlightened Citizen, being on a voidship is a lot like being on the Starship Enterprise. Most of the time you know exactly how the world works, and then suddenly a bunch of children show up and now your communications officer has aged 50 years and your helmsman is trying to figure out how to pilot through a field of starship sized knives.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T11:09:41-07:00","id":1148371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine that for an Enlightened Citizen, being on a voidship is a lot like being on the Starship Enterprise. Most of the time you know exactly how the world works, and then suddenly a bunch of children show up and now your communications officer has aged 50 years and your helmsman is trying to figure out how to pilot through a field of starship sized knives. </div> </div> </div>I imagine the main characters (the captain, the medic, the chief engineer etc.) being Enlightened , while the support staff (that security guy with the red/yellow shirt) being Extraordinary or just heavily Conditioned Citizen of the kind that can use &quot;special weapons&quot; and stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T11:40:56-07:00","id":1148390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1148010#post1148010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference being Vietnam and Afghanistan are more or less worthless chunks of the map and the Guerilla force are the natives to that map.<br /> <br /> A more apt comparison would be the Modern US invading India in the middle of British Occupation.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about the newly dubbed Americans versus the British for the US Revolutionary War? Neither was native, but one had a more heavily invested interest in changing it how THEY saw fit instead of how the OTHER SIDE saw fit. The Americans weren't using a lot of traditional tactics, especially early on, and they were wholloping one of the most formidable military forces in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T16:05:47-07:00","id":1148461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1148314#post1148314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems a little vague as to whether the VEs can or do staff their Void Ships with Sympathizers. I mean, I guess if you want to staff your ship with your Cult? That seems a little weird and kinda Heaven's Gate-y. Or, at the very least, fairly Tradition-like (So... Magic Bus-y? Bednobs-and-Broomsticks-y? Chitty-chitty-bang-bang-like?) Does indoctrination go THAT deep into a Sleeper's psyche? Or is there a Reality Zone where appropriate Sleepers can get the lowdown and then they stay on that wavelength through their entire tour in Conventional Space? And, if you do have them, doesn't that mean you CAN'T effectively take your Void Ship into the Ether? If you've got them primed for Conventional Space, they are going to be Sleepers again when you start doing &amp;quot;woo-woo we're going into SUB-SPACE now....&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> There seemed to be the heavy implication that, where appropriate, the crew could be Enlightened Citizens. You wouldn't want your engineer or pilot to be one, unless you were damn sure that nothing out of spec was going to go wrong on a mission. (Meaning &amp;quot;Never&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Probably not the captain, or effectively, most, if not all of the bridge crew. The Tech guys and the marines. They might be safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Indoctrination level 8 explicitly makes the indoctrinated not count as sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T19:38:19-07:00","id":1148491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century?p=1148371#post1148371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine the main characters (the captain, the medic, the chief engineer etc.) being Enlightened , while the support staff (that security guy with the red/yellow shirt) being Extraordinary or just heavily Conditioned Citizen of the kind that can use &quot;special weapons&quot; and stuff</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is pretty much how I see it. Your &quot;main characters' (kirk, spock, Picard, Data, etc) would be your mages. Your reoccuring specialists would be your enlightened citizens and there'd be plenty of redshirts. Of course those redshirts are coloniel Marines...<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes the Traditions might have their cults/consors/etc with them but the Technocracy in general has MUCH larger extended footprint of Extraordinary citizens, Killbots, and proles. So there are more mages in the Traditions but even counting consors, allies, familiars, cults the Technocracy easily out numbers them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:43:32-07:00","id":1150322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146994-how-soe-could-hold-their-line-against-void-engineers-for-a-century#post1146994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (...) against ceaseless onslaughts of the Void Engineers?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be easier to understand how the Sons of the Ether might have held against the Void Engineers if you take into account that their onslaught is not ceaseless. They have a limited amount of personel, and a limited amount of Awakened Void Engineers. They also have a limited amount of resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"